<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Egypt</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Egyptian</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Egypt is a country in north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a> centred on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nile">Nile</a> valley, one of the oldest centres of civilisation. Its wealth and position made it a prize for many empires: it was the core of the Egyptian Empire <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-kingdom-of-egypt">New Kingdom</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ptolemaic-kingdom">Ptolemaic Empire</a>, and was ruled by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/achaemenid-empire">Achaemenids</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Romans</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantines</a>, Arab <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliphates</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fatimid-caliphate">Fatimids</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ayyubid-empire">Ayyubids</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mamluk">Mamluks</a> and, later, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>. It also features in the histories of neighbours such as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kushite-empire">Kushite Empire</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/darfur-sultanate">Darfur Sultanate</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/egypt.jpg" alt="Egypt" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: See File history below for details. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Egypt.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
